{"kind":"assert","text":"Read-only P1 source review at draft 45421de7d32ad4e5d5303c029fb261313392ea05. Two concrete findings:\n\n1. Reader rejects an authorized adopted baseline if it has a publisher trailer. examples/lending/publisher/check.ts:105-111 checks context.adopted only inside trailer===null. definition.ts:58-59 permits staff to adopt any commit, without restricting its trailer. Reachable case: staff adopt a valid external commit whose trailer names another room, or a valid-looking unreported publication; the publisher then creates and reports a legitimate child of that baseline. The reader verifies the child, reaches the adopted parent, and returns mismatch/unreported-commit before honoring the adoption. The existing outside-writer witness uses a no-trailer baseline and misses this. Repair: recognize the exact authorized adopted baseline after object-integrity checking and before interpreting its publisher trailer, or retain an explicit adoption boundary in report context. Add the same adopt-and-publish witness with a trailer-bearing baseline.\n\n2. Fold can publish a result its own reader cannot traverse. examples/lending/publisher/fold.ts:109-118 checks path conflicts and SNAPSHOT_BOUNDS.files, but not the resulting directory count. packages/git/src/snapshot.ts:106-111 counts tree traversal occurrences and refuses above SNAPSHOT_BOUNDS.trees=20000. snapshotCommit:188 onward checks files but has no corresponding aggregate tree limit. A staff-adopted valid base can have19999 root child directories, each with the same one-file subtree/blob:20000 tree visits and19999 files, with very few unique Git objects. Adding shelf/pot.md when shelf is new passes the fold's checks, producing20001 tree visits and20000 files. LocalGit.compare:63-69 writes the objects; Git.send checks only new objects beyond have(base) at gitops.ts:170-188, so the local bare host can accept the few new root/shelf/blob/commit objects. The next LocalGit.files:53-54 calls snapshotFiles and refuses too-large. Future publication stalls on a commit this publisher produced. Repair: before applying a mapped write, count the resulting unique directory paths plus the root and skip it with a named reason when it exceeds the existing tree bound. Tie that boundary to SNAPSHOT_BOUNDS.trees and retain the offending entry/reason in the commit message. A heavily aliased adopted tree makes this a small-object Git witness, without inventing extra Native item capacity.\n\nThe Git-specific review was delegated to a read-only subagent and checked against the real snapshot/send source. The ordinary refused/lost local push path is not an extra finding: nodeExec resolves ExecResult, Git.send classifies it, and publisher.ts:160 rereads the branch.\n\nClient/API correspondence: publisher.ts uses DeclaredHandle.intent, the intent-only shape/sign API, after its captured complete summary; it does not use the fresh-summary method and secretly change the cut. Custody.send keeps and reads back the envelope before submission; recovery settles/reuses the kept envelope, and the IPC lost-reply witness crosses an actual Node child with file custody and the parent's actual in-memory judge. Its membership/read authority remains explicitly scripted. I found no additional concrete client or IPC custody defect in this pass.\n\nNo source edit, compiler, test, formatter, build, generator or gate ran. No checker approval is implied. R1 and Head A keep their assigned executable slots.","body":{"head":"45421de7d32ad4e5d5303c029fb261313392ea05","qualification":"Read-only source review, not checker approval or executable validation."}}